<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Jack Leary — Home Prototype v2</title>
<style>
  /* League Mono — real font files, copied from the LeagueMono-2.300 folder
     into src/fonts/league-mono/ so the site is self-contained (no external
     font service needed, unlike every other font this project has tried).
     Open-source (OFL), so this one's fully resolved, not a placeholder. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: "League Mono";
    src: url("/fonts/league-mono/LeagueMono-Thin.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 100;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "League Mono";
    src: url("/fonts/league-mono/LeagueMono-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: "League Mono";
    src: url("/fonts/league-mono/LeagueMono-ExtraBold.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 800;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  /* League Spartan — new header/display typeface, self-hosted the same
     way as League Mono (real file, copied from the LeagueSpartan-2.220
     folder into src/fonts/league-spartan/). Only ExtraBold is needed
     since every header/title on the site uses weight 800. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: "League Spartan";
    src: url("/fonts/league-spartan/LeagueSpartan-ExtraBold.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 800;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
</style>
<style>
  /*
    PROTOTYPE NOTES (read me first):

    "New Website 2" — a full restart on visual direction per your new style
    guide (black bg, sharp corners, red/yellow/blue accents). This is a NEW
    file, separate from prototypes/intro-prototype.html (the falling-images
    piece) — nothing there has been touched.

    FONT — League Mono, real font files (OFL, self-hosted, not a
    placeholder). Body/nav use Thin (100); the "JACK LEARY" heading uses
    ExtraBold (800).

    THIS ROUND'S CHANGES — bio text box + portrait video are gone
    entirely (both were anchored to that box, so removing the text
    orphaned the portrait too — say the word if you want the portrait
    video living somewhere else and I'll re-home it). In their place:

    - A one-line SUBHEADING under the name, styled exactly like the nav
      links (same font weight/size/tracking) — copy is a placeholder
      ("MULTIDISCIPLINARY DESIGNER — LOS ANGELES") pulled loosely from
      the old bio text; swap it for whatever you want it to say.
    - --side-pad cut in half (was clamp(24px,6vw,100px), now
      clamp(12px,3vw,50px)) — nav/subheading sit closer to the edges.
    - "JACK LEARY" no longer has the lava-lamp gradient hover at all —
      plain white text now, dropped to 75% opacity, and it breaks out of
      the side padding entirely to run flush edge-to-edge (the
      left:50%/-50vw full-bleed trick, safe because html/body already
      have overflow-x:hidden). The 5% hover scale-up is untouched.
    - A new full-viewport PROJECT GALLERY sits behind everything as the
      page's background: one project photo at a time, cover-fit, with a
      dark scrim so nav/name/captions stay legible over any photo.
      Scrolling (mouse wheel) steps through it one project at a time
      instead of scrolling the page — page scroll is fully captured for
      now since this is the only content on the page; once Work/Contact/
      Archive sections exist below this'll need to hand scroll back over
      once you run out of slides.

    CAPTION LAYOUT (updated) — the bottom caption is now a mirror of the
    top nav bar: a 3-column grid (year / title / focus) using the same
    --side-pad on both edges, so YEAR sits under WORK's left edge and
    FOCUS sits under ARCHIVE's right edge, with the title truly centered
    between them (grid's 1fr/auto/1fr, not flex space-between, so an
    uneven year/focus length can't throw the title off-center). Title
    text is sized like body copy rather than the old giant display size,
    still styled like the nav (thin weight, uppercase, tracked) so the
    whole row reads as one family with the top nav. The title is now a
    real link to that project's page — wired up for Surf and Great Ideas
    of Humanity (pages already exist); the other four projects don't
    have pages yet, so their links are inert "#" placeholders until
    those pages exist.

    PROJECT GALLERY DATA — see the PROJECTS array in the script below.
    Each entry is { slug, title, year, focus, ext, count }. Images live
    at src/images/preview/<slug>/01.<ext>, 02.<ext>, ... — built from
    whatever was already sitting in src/images/project_preview/, one
    per project so far. Title is a straight read of the project name;
    YEAR and MAIN FOCUS are both placeholders ("20XX" / "Main focus —
    TBD") since I don't have real copy for those yet — this is the part
    we go through together, project by project. When you drop in more
    preview images for a project, name them sequentially (02.<ext>,
    03.<ext>, ...) inside that project's folder and just bump its
    `count` in the array — no other code changes needed.
  */

  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  :root {
    --black:  #000000;
    --white:  #ffffff;
    --red:    #eb1c1c;
    --yellow: #f0e100;
    --blue:   #48acf0;

    /* Halved from clamp(24px, 6vw, 100px) per latest request. */
    --side-pad: clamp(12px, 3vw, 50px);
    --font-header: "League Spartan", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-body:   "League Mono", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, monospace;
  }

  html, body {
    background: var(--black);
    color: var(--white);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 100;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /* Sharp corners everywhere — no rounded edges anywhere in this design. */
  * { border-radius: 0 !important; }

  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }

  /* ---------- PROJECT GALLERY (full-bleed scroll background) ---------- */

  .project-gallery {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--black);
  }

  .project-gallery .slide {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.8s ease;
  }

  .project-gallery .slide.active {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .gallery-scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* No more edge-to-edge spread — year / title / focus now sit together
     as one centered cluster (still at vertical middle of the page), all
     lined up at the same font-size/weight/tracking so they read as one
     continuous line rather than three mismatched pieces. */
  /* The whole cluster (year — title — focus) is now one link straight to
     the project page. On hover it turns into a solid color-filled box in
     the slide's assigned accent (red/blue/yellow) — sharp corners, per
     the site's style guide, not a pill. */
  .gallery-caption {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(10px, 1.6vh, 16px) clamp(20px, 3vw, 36px);
    background-color: transparent;
    transition: background-color 0.4s ease, transform 0.4s ease;
  }

  .gallery-year,
  .gallery-focus,
  .gallery-title-link,
  .caption-dash {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 100;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 15px);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: color 0.4s ease, opacity 0.4s ease;
  }

  .gallery-year,
  .gallery-focus,
  .caption-dash {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .gallery-caption:hover {
    transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1.05);
  }
  .gallery-caption.hover-red:hover   { background-color: var(--red); }
  .gallery-caption.hover-yellow:hover { background-color: var(--yellow); }
  .gallery-caption.hover-blue:hover  { background-color: var(--blue); }

  .gallery-caption:hover .gallery-year,
  .gallery-caption:hover .gallery-focus,
  .gallery-caption:hover .gallery-title-link,
  .gallery-caption:hover .caption-dash {
    color: var(--black);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* ---------- NAV ---------- */

  .nav {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vh, 40px) var(--side-pad) 0;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .nav a {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 100;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 15px);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-8px);
    animation: navIn 0.6s ease forwards;
    transition: color 0.4s ease, transform 0.4s ease;
  }
  .nav a:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px) scale(1.08);
  }
  .nav a:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0.45s; } /* WORK — appears last (rightmost fires first) */
  .nav a:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.225s; } /* CONTACT */
  .nav a:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0s; }     /* ARCHIVE — appears first */

  /* No longer scoped to .nav a — the gallery title links reuse these too. */
  .hover-red:hover    { color: var(--red); }
  .hover-yellow:hover { color: var(--yellow); }
  .hover-blue:hover   { color: var(--blue); }

  @keyframes navIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-8px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* ---------- HERO ---------- */

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1; /* sits above .project-gallery (z-index: 0) */
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end; /* name + subheading now anchor to the bottom of the page */
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vh, 1.5rem);
    /* Bottom padding cut way down so the name sits lower, closer to the
       very edge of the viewport. */
    padding: 8vh var(--side-pad) clamp(8px, 1.5vh, 20px);
    /* .hero has no clickable content of its own (name/subheading are
       plain text), but its full-height flex box was sitting on top of
       .gallery-caption (which lives underneath, inside the fixed
       .project-gallery layer) and silently eating all its clicks/hovers.
       Turning off pointer-events here lets clicks pass through to
       whatever is actually underneath. */
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-name {
    /* No longer a full-bleed breakout — "JACK LEARY" now sits inside
       .hero's own side padding just like everything else on the page
       (nav, gallery caption), so its left/right edges line up exactly
       with WORK and ARCHIVE instead of running flush to the viewport
       edge and getting visually clipped there. fitHeroName() below
       still scaleX's the name to fill this (now narrower) container
       edge-to-edge, so it automatically stretches to the new width. */
    width: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
    line-height: 0.86;
    text-align: center;
    position: relative; /* so .subheading can center itself on top of the name */
  }

  .hero-name .stretch {
    display: inline-block;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transform-origin: center top;
    font-family: var(--font-header);
    font-weight: 800; /* League Mono ExtraBold */
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* Font size + tracking reverted back to the original — only opacity
       stays down at 45% from that round. fitHeroName() below still
       scaleX's the name to fill the container edge-to-edge; there's no
       hover scale-up any more (removed per an earlier request). */
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 15vw, 11.5rem);
    color: var(--white);
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: default;
  }

  /* Now centered directly on top of the name (both axes) instead of
     sitting on its own line below it. */
  .subheading {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 100;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 15px);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: center;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translate(-50%, calc(-50% - 8px));
    animation: subheadingIn 0.6s ease forwards;
    animation-delay: 0.6s; /* after the name has settled in */
  }

  @keyframes subheadingIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%, calc(-50% - 8px)); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); }
  }

  /* ---------- MOBILE ---------- */

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero-name .line { display: block; }
    .nav { padding-top: 20px; }
    .nav a { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
    .gallery-title { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 7vw, 2.2rem); }
  }

  /* ---------- CONTACT OVERLAY (blue/red/yellow oval, drops from top) ---- */

  .contact-overlay {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.72);
    z-index: 200;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
  }
  .contact-overlay.open {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: all;
  }

  .contact-oval {
    position: fixed;
    top: 8vh;
    left: 50%;
    width: min(56vw, 360px);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3.3;
    border-radius: 50% !important;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--blue) 0%, var(--red) 52%, var(--yellow) 100%);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(6px, 1vh, 10px);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 9% 12%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -140%);
    transition: transform 0.75s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
    z-index: 201;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }
  .contact-overlay.open .contact-oval {
    transform: translate(-50%, 0);
  }

  .contact-oval .contact-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.8vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--black);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .contact-oval .contact-email {
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.3vw, 15px);
    color: var(--black);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .contact-oval .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.8vw, 24px);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .contact-oval .contact-links a {
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--black);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    transition: opacity 0.25s ease;
  }
  .contact-oval .contact-links a:hover {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .contact-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 8%;
    right: 14%;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    font-family: var(--font-caption);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 100;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--black);
    cursor: pointer;
    opacity: 0.55;
    transition: opacity 0.25s ease;
  }
  .contact-close:hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .contact-oval {
      width: min(76vw, 300px);
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1.15;
      padding: 13% 11%;
      top: 10vh;
    }
    .contact-oval .contact-links {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
    }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <section class="project-gallery" id="project-gallery">
    <div id="gallery-slides"></div>
    <div class="gallery-scrim"></div>
    <a href="#" class="gallery-caption" id="gallery-caption">
      <span class="gallery-year" id="gallery-year"></span>
      <span class="caption-dash">—</span>
      <span class="gallery-title-link" id="gallery-title-link"></span>
      <span class="caption-dash">—</span>
      <span class="gallery-focus" id="gallery-focus"></span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="/work/" class="hover-red">Work</a>
    <a href="#contact" class="hover-yellow">Contact</a>
    <a href="/archive/" class="hover-blue">Archive</a>
  </nav>

  <header class="hero">
    <h1 class="hero-name">
      <span class="stretch" id="stretch-name">
        <span class="line">JACK</span><span class="line" style="display:inline">&nbsp;LEARY</span>
      </span>
      <p class="subheading">Multidisciplinary Designer — Los Angeles</p>
    </h1>
  </header>

<script>
(function () {
  // ---- Name: stretch to fill the full-bleed width -------------------------
  // Same "measure natural width, scaleX up to container width" trick used
  // elsewhere on the site. .hero-name is now 100vw (full-bleed breakout),
  // so this automatically stretches the name edge-to-edge instead of just
  // to the padded content width. On mobile the two <span class="line">
  // words stack (see the media query) and each one gets measured/stretched
  // independently.
  const heroName = document.querySelector(".hero-name");
  const stretchEl = document.getElementById("stretch-name");
  const lineEls = stretchEl.querySelectorAll(".line");

  function isMobile() {
    return window.matchMedia("(max-width: 700px)").matches;
  }

  // Base scaleX from the stretch-to-fill trick — stored so the hover
  // scale-up (5%) can be combined with it instead of overwriting it.
  let desktopScaleX = 1;

  function fitHeroName() {
    const containerWidth = heroName.clientWidth;

    if (isMobile()) {
      stretchEl.style.transform = "none";
      lineEls.forEach((line) => {
        line.style.transform = "none";
        line.style.transformOrigin = "center top";
        const natural = line.getBoundingClientRect().width;
        if (natural > 0) {
          line.style.transform = `scaleX(${containerWidth / natural})`;
        }
      });
    } else {
      lineEls.forEach((line) => { line.style.transform = "none"; });
      stretchEl.style.transform = "none";
      const natural = stretchEl.getBoundingClientRect().width;
      // No more hover scale-up, so no headroom to bake in — scale
      // straight to the full container width.
      desktopScaleX = natural > 0 ? containerWidth / natural : 1;
      stretchEl.style.transform = `scaleX(${desktopScaleX})`;
    }
  }

  window.addEventListener("resize", fitHeroName);
  fitHeroName();
  if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) {
    document.fonts.ready.then(fitHeroName);
  }

  // ---- Project gallery: scroll-driven background slideshow ---------------
  // PROJECTS is the thing to edit as we go through these together — title
  // is a straight read of the project name, year/focus are both
  // placeholders. `count` images are expected at
  // src/images/preview/<slug>/01.<ext> .. 0<count>.<ext> — bump `count`
  // once more numbered images are dropped in that folder.
  // `page` is the project's own prototype page — "#" is a placeholder for
  // projects that don't have one built yet. `hover` cycles through the
  // three accent colors (same hover-red/yellow/blue classes the nav
  // uses) so the title link picks up one of them on hover, same as WORK/
  // CONTACT/ARCHIVE do.
  const PROJECTS = [
    { slug: "puck-and-chuck",           title: "Puck + Chuck",               year: "2026", focus: "Brand Identity", ext: "png", count: 2, page: "/projects/puck-and-chuck/", hover: "hover-blue" },
    { slug: "surf",                     title: "Surf",                       year: "2024", focus: "Editorial Presentation", ext: "jpg", count: 2, page: "/projects/surf/",        hover: "hover-red" },
    { slug: "hangul",                   title: "Hangul",                     year: "2026", focus: "Poster Design", ext: "png", count: 2, page: "/projects/hangul/",     hover: "hover-red" },
    { slug: "adobe-firefly",            title: "Adobe Firefly",              year: "2026", focus: "Brand Identity", ext: "png", count: 2, page: "/projects/adobe-firefly/", hover: "hover-yellow" },
    { slug: "over-the-hump",            title: "Over the Hump",              year: "2024-2025", focus: "Social Media Design", ext: "jpg", count: 2, page: "/projects/over-the-hump/", hover: "hover-blue" },
    { slug: "great-ideas-of-humanity",   title: "Great Ideas of Humanity",    year: "2025", focus: "Poster Design", ext: "png", count: 2, page: "/projects/great-ideas-of-humanity/", hover: "hover-yellow" },
  ];

  // Flatten each project's numbered images into one ordered list of
  // slides. Multiple images under one project stay grouped together and
  // keep showing that same project's title/year/focus as you step through
  // them, only changing caption once you cross into the next project.
  const SLIDES = [];
  PROJECTS.forEach((project) => {
    for (let i = 1; i <= project.count; i++) {
      const num = String(i).padStart(2, "0");
      SLIDES.push({
        image: `/images/preview/${project.slug}/${num}.${project.ext}`,
        title: project.title,
        year: project.year,
        focus: project.focus,
        page: project.page,
        hover: project.hover,
      });
    }
  });

  const slidesContainer = document.getElementById("gallery-slides");
  const captionLinkEl = document.getElementById("gallery-caption");
  const yearEl = document.getElementById("gallery-year");
  const titleLinkEl = document.getElementById("gallery-title-link");
  const focusEl = document.getElementById("gallery-focus");

  const slideEls = SLIDES.map((slide) => {
    const div = document.createElement("div");
    div.className = "slide";
    div.style.backgroundImage = `url("${slide.image}")`;
    slidesContainer.appendChild(div);
    return div;
  });

  let current = 0;

  function showSlide(index) {
    slideEls.forEach((el, i) => el.classList.toggle("active", i === index));
    const s = SLIDES[index];
    yearEl.textContent = s.year;
    titleLinkEl.textContent = s.title;
    focusEl.textContent = s.focus;
    captionLinkEl.href = s.page;
    captionLinkEl.classList.remove("hover-red", "hover-yellow", "hover-blue");
    captionLinkEl.classList.add(s.hover);
  }

  if (SLIDES.length > 0) {
    showSlide(0);
  }

  // Scroll (wheel) steps one slide at a time, with a short cooldown so a
  // single trackpad/wheel gesture doesn't blow through several slides at
  // once — this is the whole page's scroll for now since there's nothing
  // below it yet; once Work/Contact/Archive exist this'll need to release
  // the scroll-jack once you run past the last slide.
  let cooldown = false;
  const COOLDOWN_MS = 700;

  function step(direction) {
    if (cooldown || SLIDES.length === 0) return;
    // Wraps both directions now — scrolling past the last project (GIOH)
    // loops back to the first (Puck + Chuck), and scrolling back past the
    // first loops to the last, so it reads as one continuous loop instead
    // of dead-ending at either end.
    current = (current + direction + SLIDES.length) % SLIDES.length;
    showSlide(current);
    cooldown = true;
    setTimeout(() => { cooldown = false; }, COOLDOWN_MS);
  }

  window.addEventListener("wheel", (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    step(e.deltaY > 0 ? 1 : -1);
  }, { passive: false });

  // Touch swipe (mobile/trackpad-less testing) — up-swipe advances, same
  // as scrolling down would.
  let touchStartY = null;
  window.addEventListener("touchstart", (e) => {
    touchStartY = e.touches[0].clientY;
  }, { passive: true });
  window.addEventListener("touchend", (e) => {
    if (touchStartY === null) return;
    const deltaY = touchStartY - e.changedTouches[0].clientY;
    if (Math.abs(deltaY) > 30) step(deltaY > 0 ? 1 : -1);
    touchStartY = null;
  }, { passive: true });

  // Arrow keys — convenient while testing at a desk.
  window.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
    if (e.key === "ArrowDown" || e.key === "ArrowRight") step(1);
    if (e.key === "ArrowUp" || e.key === "ArrowLeft") step(-1);
  });
})();
</script>

